.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SOCKET 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm socket
.Nd create an endpoint for communication
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn socket "int domain" "int type" "int protocol"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn socket
system call creates an unconnected socket and returns a descriptor for it.
.Pp
The
.Fa domain
selects the address family:
.Bl -tag -width AF_UNIX -offset indent
.It Dv AF_UNIX
local sockets, also called
.Dv AF_LOCAL ;
see
.Xr unix 4 .
.It Dv AF_INET
Internet version 4 protocols.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fa type
selects the semantics of communication:
.Bl -tag -width SOCK_SEQPACKET -offset indent
.It Dv SOCK_STREAM
a reliable, ordered, connected byte stream without record boundaries.
.It Dv SOCK_DGRAM
messages of limited size, each delivered whole or not at all.
.It Dv SOCK_SEQPACKET
a connected stream of records, which keep their boundaries
.Pq Dv AF_UNIX No only .
.It Dv SOCK_RAW
raw access to a network protocol
.Pq Dv AF_INET No with Dv IPPROTO_ICMP No only .
.El
.Pp
Either or both of these flags may be OR'd into
.Fa type :
.Bl -tag -width SOCK_NONBLOCK -offset indent
.It Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
set the close-on-exec flag on the new descriptor.
.It Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK
set
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
on the new open file description.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fa protocol
is 0 for the default protocol of the domain and type.
The supported combinations are:
.Bl -column "AF_INET" "SOCK_SEQPACKET" "0 or IPPROTO_TCP" -offset indent
.It Sy Domain Ta Sy Type Ta Sy Protocol
.It Dv AF_UNIX Ta Dv SOCK_STREAM Ta 0
.It Dv AF_UNIX Ta Dv SOCK_DGRAM Ta 0
.It Dv AF_UNIX Ta Dv SOCK_SEQPACKET Ta 0
.It Dv AF_INET Ta Dv SOCK_STREAM Ta 0 or Dv IPPROTO_TCP
.It Dv AF_INET Ta Dv SOCK_DGRAM Ta 0 or Dv IPPROTO_UDP
.It Dv AF_INET Ta Dv SOCK_RAW Ta Dv IPPROTO_ICMP
.El
.Pp
A connected socket is made with
.Xr connect 2
on one side and
.Xr listen 2
and
.Xr accept 2
on the other, or both at once with
.Xr socketpair 2 .
Data is sent with
.Xr send 2 ,
.Xr sendto 2 ,
.Xr sendmsg 2
or
.Xr write 2 ,
and received with
.Xr recv 2 ,
.Xr recvfrom 2 ,
.Xr recvmsg 2
or
.Xr read 2 ;
.Xr read 2
and
.Xr write 2
on a socket behave as
.Xr recvmsg 2
and
.Xr sendmsg 2
with no address, no control data and no flags.
Options are read and set with
.Xr getsockopt 2
and
.Xr setsockopt 2 ,
and
.Xr shutdown 2
closes one direction or both.
.Pp
A blocking call on a socket waits with interrupts enabled.
A signal caught during the wait makes it fail with
.Er EINTR ,
or restarts it if the handler was installed with
.Dv SA_RESTART ,
no data has been transferred, and no timeout
.Pq Dv SO_RCVTIMEO , SO_SNDTIMEO
is set.
.Pp
A socket is readable for
.Xr poll 2
and
.Xr select 2
when data, end-of-file, a pending error or, on a listening socket, a
connection is waiting; writable when a send would not block; and reports
.Dv POLLHUP
once both directions are shut down or the peer has gone.
.Xr fstat 2
on a socket reports
.Dv S_IFSOCK .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success
.Fn socket
returns the new descriptor, the lowest one free.
Otherwise it returns \-1 and sets
.Va errno .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAFNOSUPPORT
The
.Fa domain
is not supported.
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system limit on open files,
.Va kern.maxfiles ,
has been reached.
.It Bq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT
The
.Fa type
or
.Fa protocol
is not supported in the domain.
.It Bq Er EPROTOTYPE
The
.Fa protocol
exists, but under another type
.Pq Dv IPPROTO_TCP No with Dv SOCK_DGRAM , for example .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr accept 2 ,
.Xr bind 2 ,
.Xr connect 2 ,
.Xr getsockname 2 ,
.Xr getsockopt 2 ,
.Xr listen 2 ,
.Xr recvmsg 2 ,
.Xr sendmsg 2 ,
.Xr shutdown 2 ,
.Xr socketpair 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn socket
system call conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
and
.Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK
are in
IEEE Std 1003.1-2024.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn socket
system call first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
In OxideBSD every address family plugs into one socket layer through a
protocol switch, as in the BSDs.
